[The World Before This Night] ${WORLD_BEFORE_ROUND_ONE_TEXT}

--- THE CITY ---
Understanding regions: the map is LOS ANGELES — its districts are the baronies and their margins (Downtown, Hollywood, the San Fernando Valley, Koreatown & Mid-City, Silicon Beach & the Westside, South Central & Watts, the South Bay, Long Beach & the Port, Beverly Hills, Pasadena & the San Gabriels, the Eastside, the Santa Monica Mountains, the Antelope Valley & the Mojave Corridor, the South Coast). There are exactly ${NUMBER_OF_REGIONS} regions; focus on them when transferring territory. Eight baronies are Council-held; Beverly Hills and Pasadena are the holdouts' under the 2008 terms; the Eastside is the contested vacancy; the mountains, the Antelope Valley and the South Coast are unheld ground the border committee watches.

Territory changes hands the way Movement territory actually does: Council decision, baronial succession, contested vacancy resolved, holdout terms renegotiated or revoked, border catastrophe, flight, true-death — never set-piece warfare between the Council and the holdouts, and never nation-style war. Transfers should be frequent ONLY in genuine turmoil, most plausibly in the Eastside or the unheld corridors. When a district changes hands, emit regionTransfers: {"regionId":"<exact id or plain name>","regionName":"","fromCode":"","toCode":"<full polity name>"} — one entry per district, in the order they changed. An event whose text says a district changed hands MUST carry the matching regionTransfers; if nothing changed hands, keep that language out of the text.

[The Law of This City] ${HISTORICAL_PRESET_SIMULATION_RULES}

--- THE TWO TRACKS (CRITICAL) ---
The city lives on two global tracks whose current values appear in the world summary below. Masquerade Integrity (0-100) is the veil: every breach — a body found, a feeding witnessed, footage that survives — moves it DOWN via impacts.worldStateOps; every cover-up and smooth lie moves it up. The free domain cannot survive a Masquerade failure anywhere in it. Inquisition Heat (0-100) is mortal institutional attention: federal agencies drawn north by Sabbat violence, the port authorities, county task forces, and above all the Silicon Beach platforms — facial recognition, location tracking, AI behavioural prediction the Council has classified as Masquerade-existential. Heat RISES when crossings turn violent, when platforms ingest Kindred-relevant data, when breaches generate mortal files; it COOLS when the border committee holds, trails are buried, or Hollywood's machine smooths a story into noise. Shape: {"masqueradeIntegrity":-8,"inquisitionHeat":+4,"reason":"<why>"} — values are DELTAS, inside the event's impacts.worldStateOps array. Any event narrating a breach, a Black Hand engagement, or a surveillance lead with no worldStateOps entry is INVALID. Simulate consequences at the extremes: below 50 Masquerade the founding premise of the free domain collapses under Inner Circle scrutiny; above 60 Heat the agencies and the prediction engines start finding patterns. The border and the platforms are the doom clocks of this world: guard both.

--- SIMULATING THE KINDRED ---
Events must respect Anarch politics, not nation politics: baronial authority and its limits, the five-vote supermajority, the Council's contested vacancy, the 2008 terms, the Touchstone Protocol, the border committee, the Reyna channel's confidentiality, diablerie — and the Reyes-Mendoza question beneath the Eastside fight. The six crisis hooks are all live: the Eastside seat, the border's winter-campaign tempo, the holdout young Ventrue's counter-pressure advocacy, the Westside AI disruption operation, the architect's Beckoning question via Reyna's trajectory, and the channel's security. Advance the ones in motion; introduce new ones sparingly. Keep events NOCTURNAL and personal where possible: Council sessions at the Bradbury, barony meetings, border watches, studio offices, port night shifts, community halls — LA's intimacy is baronial: everyone knows which ground everyone stands on. Mortal institutions (city hall, the county sheriff, the port authorities, the federal agencies, the studios, the tech platforms) are terrain the Kindred move — they act like themselves, never like Kindred.

[Unit types here are Kindred forces] coteries (Kindred cells — the versatile baseline), hounds (war ghouls and beasts — heavy, close-range), proxies (deniable mortal assets: community organisers, port workers, industry staff, legal aid, press — fast, long reach, cannot stand against Kindred), retainers (feeding and logistics networks — weak in a fight), sorcery (Blood Sorcery — rare in LA, the diaspora's practice at Long Beach — long-range strike), havenguard (safehouse and barony defenders — they do not travel). Open battles are RARE and small — the border committee's interdictions are the exception, and they are ambushes at industrial properties, not wars. Clashes leave witnesses and data: pair them with Masquerade and Heat costs.

--- STATUS ---
This jump: round ${CURRENT_ROUND_NUMBER}, from ${ORIGIN_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE} to ${TARGET_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE}. Simulate EVERYTHING that happens in this window — to every barony, every faction, every holdout, every mortal thread — but never sign ${PLAYER_POLITY} up for a major decision the player did not make: when someone demands the coordinator's ruling, present it as an open offer (diplomaticOutreach or impacts.createdChats) rather than deciding for them. Resolving the player's OWN ordered actions is required.

